line	<str>Make your way to the sapphire gate north of the main block.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run to the most north-western room filled with 25 chests.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest directly beside the west door. It should say "Vials".</str>
line	
line	<str>Attempt to open it and enter the password LIES for an emerald key.</str>
line	
line	<str>After you leave the room, Jhallan may attack you. Re-entering the room with the chests may get him to disappear, and Protect from Magic greatly reduces the damage he does. When opening some doors, Jhallan may re-appear and attack again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run east and unblock the crevice. Squeeze through.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head directly south one room and open the emerald gate in the room with seven beds.</str>
line	
line	<str>Click on the chest in the south-east part of the room. Enter the combination UP, RIGHT, LEFT, DOWN, RIGHT, UP for a ruby key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the main block and open the ruby gate to the south-west</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the first cell with a chest in it. Enter the passcode WRATH for a diamond key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head back to the main block where the assassin is. Talk to him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the conversation is over, enter the cell and collect your items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the assassin again. When this conversation ends, he will teleport away.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Refugee Camp, and search the pack next to the centre pillar to light the firecrackers.</str>
line	
line	<str>Survive Jhallan's onslaught until the assassin arrives. Pray Protect from Magic and run around the centre pillar to avoid being hit. Occasionally you will be teleported and frozen. When the illusions appear, kill them to avoid taking damage (1 Hitpoint each).</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare to fight Duke Sucellus. You can go to a bank and return safely.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Dragonstone Gate, in the very far north-east section of the prison (NOT IN ADMINISTRATION AREA).</str>
line	
line	<str>Once inside the Asylum, Duke Sucellus' chamber is located directly north of you but the Duke himself is asleep. On the sides there are extremities that periodically open their eyes, their gaze emitting a red cone. You will need to run past the extremities while also avoiding stunning energy attacks emitting from the floor indicated by a shadow: If hit by the extremities, you will take large amounts of damage..</str>
line	
line	<str>Once past the extremities, there are arder and musca mushrooms, one on each site. 80+ Herblore: Pick 2 of each mushroom and use a pestle & mortar on them, under 80 herblore: pick 3 of each; afterwards make your way to the centre of the room where there are two barrels you must deposit the grounded mushrooms into. On the sides of the arena, near the middle pillars are salt deposits which you must mine: You need 12 parts of salt and each mushroom dust to fill the two barrels and obtain two Arder-musca poisons.</str>
line	
line	<str>When you have the two poisons, drink your potions and activate Piety and use the poisons on Duke Sucellus which will begin the fight. Sucellus has several attacks, most of which deal a lot of damage if they hit you:</str>
line	
line	<str>Sucellus is weak to demonbane weapons and his spike attack deals less damage than his Magic so Arclight is an ideal weapon to dispose of him. An easy way to defeat Sucellus is to equip as much Strength-boosting gear as possible and stand directly behind one of the two pillars closest to him. Every time Sucellus uses his ground slam attack, as soon as his arms hit the ground hit him and immediately run back behind the pillar, as if you were flinching him: You will take chip damage from the spikes initially spawning but with high-healing food such as Karambwan the fight is manageable. When Sucellus fires acid, run to the other side of the room while being careful not to get hit by the spikes or his arms, and when he opens his eye make sure you're hiding behind the pillar closest to you!</str>
line	
line	<str>After Sucellus is taken care of, take the key that he drops and enter the room on the west side of the main hallway. Talk with the Assassin and open the chest in the corner to receive Sucellus' medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>After obtaining the medallion, place it on the south-west Statue at the quest start location.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Ruins of Camdozaal and speak to Ramarno , located near the Smithing icon just north of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Prescott, near the bank chest south-east for a very long rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the north-western part of the ruins and attach the rope to the rock by the sinkhole.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down and activate the teleporter (link=no) on the map.</str>
line	
line	<str>Activate the teleporters whenever you pass by one.</str>
line	
line	<str>In the north-western building of the Science District, take the shadow blocker schematic and the green shadow key.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Take the <col=800000>purple shadow key</col> from the building south of the one you were in.</col>
step	108	-	Quick guide step 108
line	<str>Enter the Ancient Vault, found south-east of fairy ring DLQ or north-east of Nardah.) (Teleport: Nardah teleport|pic=Nardah teleport|size=20, Desert amulet|pic=Desert amulet 3|size=20)</str>
line	
line	<str>After finishing the conversation, inspect the four statues and the plaque.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Asgarnia Smith.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Exam Centre and speak to Terry Balando. (Teleport: Senntisten teleport|pic=Senntisten Teleport icon (mobile)|size=20)</str>
line	
line	<str>Operate the winch at the easternmost part of the Digsite. (Teleport: Digsite teleport|pic=Digsite teleport|size=20 or Digsite pendant|pic=Digsite pendant|size=20)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dr Banikan. Once the option to mine the rocks is available, you do not need to ask him any more questions.</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare for combat, and mine the nearby rocks when ready. A bronze pickaxe can be found in the crate to the north if needed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the crevice and kill the Ancient Guardian.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Dr Banikan.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the golem machine.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the crates for uncharged cells.</str>
line	
line	<str>Cast burst spells or greater on the matching totems.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use cells on altar to get charged cells.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the charged cells on the golem and solve the puzzle as seen below: File:Desert Treasure II - golem puzzle solution.png</str>
line	
line	<str>Search "Vardorvis", "Perseriya", "Sucellus", and "Whisperer".</str>
line	
line	<str>Operate the golem machine once more.</str>
line	
line	<str>Exit the military installation and speak to Elissa north of the winch.</str>
line	
line	<str>Visit the Burning Man (south-west of Xeric's Inferno teleport) in Lovakengj and speak to Barus.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the desk in the house south of the Hosidius Estate Agent (north-east of Xeric's Glade Teleport) for a strange potion and potion note. Read the note.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go south of Mount Quidamortem (Xeric's Honour teleport) or west of fairy ring BLS to the boat dock to the west. Drink the strange potion and board to get to The Stranglewood.</str>
line	
line	<str>Beware that The Stranglewood is full of high level (combat 138, 149) strangled who will root you and deal continual damage.</str>
line	
line	<str>Immediately upon arriving by boat, inspect the statue / totem nearby as it acts as a stamina potion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Follow the path south, enter the city, and talk to Kasonde after the cutscene.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go down the entry and defend Kasonde from the strangled for three minutes by building barricades, detonating satchels, and attacking them. Failing will simply start the activity over.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go upstairs and talk to Kasonde.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gather korbal herb and argian berries.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the largest pyramid at the north end of the city.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the pyramid and fight the strangled attacking Kasonde.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Kasonde.</str>
line	
line	<str>Use the korbal herb and then the Argian berries on the unfinished serum.</str>
line	
line	<str>Drink the strangler serum; the strangled will no longer root you, nor will you gain infection and be forced to restart. However, you will still take normal damage from them.</str>
line	
line	<str>Gear to fight Vardorvis, who is located in the north west snowy square. The first time you go, you need to run back down south-west across the bridge, west, and around the long way. After entering the lair once you can start to use a shortcut by going down the entry in the north-west, near where the herb was found, and then running west to the square. Vardorvis is weak against slash, and weapons such as scythe of Vitur and abyssal tentacle work well.</str>
line	
line	<str>After you've entered his area you unlock a shortcut near the boat to get back. It's the path north of the temple. You do not need to complete the boss battle to unlock this shortcut.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating Vardorvis, pick up the temple key and bring it back to Kasonde in the Temple. Be aware that you are about to fight another boss.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kasonde will attack you. Dodge his explosions and poison splats.</str>
line	
line	<str>After defeating him talk to him to find out where the medallion is, then proceed to the next room and search the stone chest for a tatty page.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the hideout with the barricade and search the stone chest in the north-east corner to obtain Vardorvis' medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the medallion to the Ancient Vault north-east of Nardah and use it on Vardorvis' statue in the north-east corner.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Guardians of the Rift minigame. This can be reached quickly via the Amulet of the Eye teleport, Minigame Teleport or via the portal in the Wizards' Tower basement (Fairy ring DIS)</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the Catalytic Guardian near the entrance and enter The Scar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill the monsters before crossing the stepping stones. Some of these can be safe spotted behind the vent in the north-west corner. Praying against melee will result in no damage taken.</str>
line	
line	<str>Attempt to board the boat and talk to Wizard Persten.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter through the passage and proceed to solve the three puzzles in each room. Leaving the Scar will reset all the puzzles already completed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Note: Because the passage that players arrive in varies, the next three sections may appear out of order for players, but all three must be completed before the passage to one of Perseriya's ships is opened. In addition, a slayer helmet or facemask are required for the second and third passages. During your third scar, you will take minimal periodic choking damage, do not AFK for extended periods outside of the puzzles (This damage does not occur in either finished or unfinished puzzles).</str>
line	
line	<str>Throughout The Scar you will find chests with scarred scraps. These restore run energy, health, and Prayer, as well as providing a stamina effect. Praying Protect from Magic is effective against the scarred lesser demons.</str>
line	
line	<str>Axon Terminal:</str>
line	
line	<str>Broken Nerve Endings (underwater):</str>
line	
line	<str>Summoning Circle:</str>
line	
line	<str>After completing the puzzles, go to the shipwreck room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Abyssal Stem (underwater):</str>
line	
line	<str>Brain Pillar:</str>
line	
line	<str>Unlit Veins:</str>
line	
line	<str>After completing the puzzles, go to the shipwreck room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Abyssal Tether:</str>
line	
line	<str>Catalyst:</str>
line	
line	<str>Damaged Growth:</str>
line	
line	<str>After completing the puzzles, go to the shipwreck room.</str>
line	
line	<str>Kill The Leviathan.</str>
line	
line	<str>After killing him leave the area to the north-east and talk to Wizard Persten again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the debris nearby on the small island and receive Perseriya's medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>Be wary that the Mysterious Figure may attack you as you attempt to return the medallion. You can cheese the Stranger by running to Nardah and using the statue to heal and restore Prayer. You need to have two combat styles to kill it, and once you do The Stranger will teleport away. NOTE: YOU CAN SPAM CLICK THE VAULT AND THE STRANGER WILL NOT FOLLOW YOU INSIDE.</str>
line	
line	<str>Bring the medallion with you back to the Ancient Vault and place it on the south-east statue.</str>
line	
line	<str>You can bring gear to fight Duke Sucellus in advance, as during the puzzle your worn items and inventory will temporarily be removed and stored.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go underneath Weiss dungeon and follow it around and north to get to the prison door.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once you get into the prison you will run north and get teleported to a cell.</str>
line	
line	<str>Inspect the wall north of the cell.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search the skeleton inside the cell to find a letter and read it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the voice in the wall again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search for a knife - it will be in the bed or bucket.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the voice in the wall again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Search for a lockpick - it will be in the bed or bucket (whichever one you haven't found something in).</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the voice in the wall again to escape.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the assassin. You must finish the conversation (they will teleport away).</str>
line	
line	<str>From point Y on the map, head to point L. Complete the puzzle to unlock it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the south-east path all the way around, and go through the gate to the refugee camp.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the gate to the south to access the room with the altar.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest in the south-east corner. Input the password 214013 to get a sapphire key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the sapphire gate north of the main block.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run to the most north-western room filled with 25 chests.</str>
line	
line	<str>Open the chest directly beside the west door. It should say "Vials".</str>
line	
line	<str>Attempt to open it and enter the password LIES for an emerald key.</str>
line	
line	<str>After you leave the room, Jhallan may attack you. Re-entering the room with the chests may get him to disappear, and Protect from Magic greatly reduces the damage he does. When opening some doors, Jhallan may re-appear and attack again.</str>
line	
line	<str>Run east and unblock the crevice. Squeeze through.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head directly south one room and open the emerald gate in the room with seven beds.</str>
line	
line	<str>Click on the chest in the south-east part of the room. Enter the combination UP, RIGHT, LEFT, DOWN, RIGHT, UP for a ruby key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to the main block and open the ruby gate to the south-west</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the first cell with a chest in it. Enter the passcode WRATH for a diamond key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head back to the main block where the assassin is. Talk to him.</str>
line	
line	<str>Once the conversation is over, enter the cell and collect your items.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to the assassin again. When this conversation ends, he will teleport away.</str>
line	
line	<str>Head to the Refugee Camp, and search the pack next to the centre pillar to light the firecrackers.</str>
line	
line	<str>Survive Jhallan's onslaught until the assassin arrives. Pray Protect from Magic and run around the centre pillar to avoid being hit. Occasionally you will be teleported and frozen. When the illusions appear, kill them to avoid taking damage (1 Hitpoint each).</str>
line	
line	<str>Prepare to fight Duke Sucellus. You can go to a bank and return safely.</str>
line	
line	<str>Enter the Dragonstone Gate, in the very far north-east section of the prison (NOT IN ADMINISTRATION AREA).</str>
line	
line	<str>Once inside the Asylum, Duke Sucellus' chamber is located directly north of you but the Duke himself is asleep. On the sides there are extremities that periodically open their eyes, their gaze emitting a red cone. You will need to run past the extremities while also avoiding stunning energy attacks emitting from the floor indicated by a shadow: If hit by the extremities, you will take large amounts of damage..</str>
line	
line	<str>Once past the extremities, there are arder and musca mushrooms, one on each site. 80+ Herblore: Pick 2 of each mushroom and use a pestle & mortar on them, under 80 herblore: pick 3 of each; afterwards make your way to the centre of the room where there are two barrels you must deposit the grounded mushrooms into. On the sides of the arena, near the middle pillars are salt deposits which you must mine: You need 12 parts of salt and each mushroom dust to fill the two barrels and obtain two Arder-musca poisons.</str>
line	
line	<str>When you have the two poisons, drink your potions and activate Piety and use the poisons on Duke Sucellus which will begin the fight. Sucellus has several attacks, most of which deal a lot of damage if they hit you:</str>
line	
line	<str>Sucellus is weak to demonbane weapons and his spike attack deals less damage than his Magic so Arclight is an ideal weapon to dispose of him. An easy way to defeat Sucellus is to equip as much Strength-boosting gear as possible and stand directly behind one of the two pillars closest to him. Every time Sucellus uses his ground slam attack, as soon as his arms hit the ground hit him and immediately run back behind the pillar, as if you were flinching him: You will take chip damage from the spikes initially spawning but with high-healing food such as Karambwan the fight is manageable. When Sucellus fires acid, run to the other side of the room while being careful not to get hit by the spikes or his arms, and when he opens his eye make sure you're hiding behind the pillar closest to you!</str>
line	
line	<str>After Sucellus is taken care of, take the key that he drops and enter the room on the west side of the main hallway. Talk with the Assassin and open the chest in the corner to receive Sucellus' medallion.</str>
line	
line	<str>After obtaining the medallion, place it on the south-west Statue at the quest start location.</str>
line	
line	<str>Make your way to the Ruins of Camdozaal and speak to Ramarno , located near the Smithing icon just north of the entrance.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Prescott, near the bank chest south-east for a very long rope.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the north-western part of the ruins and attach the rope to the rock by the sinkhole.</str>
line	
line	<str>Climb down and activate the teleporter (link=no) on the map.</str>
line	
line	<str>Activate the teleporters whenever you pass by one.</str>
line	
line	<str>In the north-western building of the Science District, take the shadow blocker schematic and the green shadow key.</str>
line	
line	<str>Take the purple shadow key from the building south of the one you were in.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Walk towards the Sunken Cathedral.</col>
